module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalExtendedCech
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.SheafifiedCechFiniteType
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Tag 099E on each slice of a cover, for a sheaf of ideals of finite type

[Stacks, Tag 099E] asks, for a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊆ 𝒪` of **finite type** on a ringed site
`(𝒞, 𝒪)`, for a map `K ⟶ 𝒪` in `D(𝒪)` whose restriction to every object carrying a finite family
generating `ℐ` there is the extended alternating Čech complex of that family, compatibly with the
maps to `𝒪`. That condition is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsGlobalExtendedCech` of `GlobalExtendedCech.lean`, and it is
proved there, with no hypotheses, for an `ℐ` generated by finitely many *global* sections.

This file proves the tag **on each slice of a covering family**, for an `ℐ` that is merely of
finite type — the tag's own hypothesis — and with no hypotheses beyond it:

> there is a family `{V_i}` of objects covering the site such that for each `i` there is a
> complex `K_i` of sheaves of `𝒪_{V_i}`-modules and a map `K_i ⟶ 𝒪_{V_i}` satisfying the
> condition of the tag for `ℐ|_{V_i}`.

Two inputs, both proved elsewhere. A finite-type sheaf of ideals is generated by finitely many
*global* sections on each slice of a covering family — that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal` of
`SheafifiedCechFiniteType.lean`, which also identifies the sheaf of ideals those sections generate
on the slice with `ℐ|_{V_i}` on the nose. And for a family of global sections the tag holds with
no hypotheses — that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isGlobalExtendedCech_idealOfGlobalSections`, applied to the
slice ringed site.

## What is left, and why it is not here

What remains is the passage from these local solutions to a single `K ⟶ 𝒪` on `𝒞`, and it is
*not* an instance of the locality of morphisms in `D(𝒪)`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`): there is no global `K` yet whose
restrictions could be compared. It is descent, and the input of the effectivity theorem
[Stacks, Tag 04TR] is a family of **isomorphisms of complexes** over the overlaps with a cocycle
condition.

The complexes exhibited above cannot supply that family.
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isEmpty_iso_sheafifiedCech_oneFamily` of
`CechDescentDatumObstruction.lean` proves that on any ringed site whose structure sheaf is not a
zero object the two constant families `(1)` and `(1, 1)` — which span the unit ideal of sections
over *every* object, so that no refinement of any covering separates them — have Čech objects
that are quasi-isomorphic over `𝒪`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.quasiIso_sheafifiedCechRestrict_oneFamily`) and **not** isomorphic
as complexes. The obstruction is a count of terms and survives every localization and base change.
Nor can the generating families be chosen coherently instead: a choice of finite generating family
transported by every ring map does not exist
(`Stacks.FunctorialCechFamily.isEmpty_functorialGenerators`).

So the complex to be glued has to be attached to the *ideal* and not to a generating family. Two
finitely generated `I, I' ⊆ ℐ(U)` generating `ℐ|_U` do span the same ideal of sections along every
arrow of a covering sieve (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_mem_sieve_span_eq`), so a model
depending only on the ideal is *literally the same* over each member of that covering and its
descent datum is the identity, with the cocycle condition vacuous. Such a model, functorial in the
ring, is exactly [Stacks, Tag 099D] — the interface
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData`, which no term of this library inhabits.

**Status.** [Stacks, Tag 099E] is proved for an arbitrary sheaf of ideals, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isGlobalExtendedCech` of `FiniteTypeExtendedCech.lean`,
and [Stacks, Tag 099F] follows from it as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete` of `FiniteTypeReflector.lean`.
Neither [Stacks, Tag 099D] nor any gluing is used there: the presheaf of Čech complexes of *all*
local generators of `ℐ` — a filtered colimit, hence a presheaf with no choice made — is
sheafified on `𝒞`, and on each slice the leg into it from the Čech complex of one generating
family is locally bijective on homology. Where the notes
below say that 099E is missing or needs gluing, they record the state of the library before
that construction.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_isGlobalExtendedCech_overIdeal`: **the condition
  of [Stacks, Tag 099E] holds on each slice of a covering family, for a sheaf of ideals of finite
  type**, with no hypotheses beyond the finite-type condition.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_isGlobalExtendedCech_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType`:
  the same at Mathlib's finite-type condition, which is the hypothesis the tag carries.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks 099E]` attribute is attached, following the precedent of
`SheafifiedCechFiniteType.lean`: the tag asserts a single complex on the site, and a family of
complexes on the slices of a cover is not that assertion. The tag is registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isGlobalExtendedCech` of `FiniteTypeExtendedCech.lean`.

The instance hypothesis `∀ U : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.over U).J CommRingCat.{u}` is the
sheafification of presheaves of commutative rings on each slice site. It is the same technical
hypothesis the slice statements of this directory carry — `section Restrict` of
`GlobalExtendedCech.lean` carries it at a single object — and it is a property of the site, not of
the sheaf of ideals: the statements of the tag are untouched by it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04TR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04TR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard additive_overFunctor

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  [∀ U : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.over U).J CommRingCat.{u}]
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099E] on each slice of a covering family, for a sheaf of ideals of finite
type.** There is a family `{V_i}` of objects covering the site such that over each `V_i` there is
a complex `K_i` of sheaves of `𝒪_{V_i}`-modules and a map `K_i ⟶ 𝒪_{V_i}` with the property the
tag asserts for `ℐ|_{V_i}`: on every object of `𝒞/V_i` carrying a finite family generating
`ℐ|_{V_i}` there, its restriction is the extended alternating Čech complex of that family in the
derived category, compatibly with the maps to the structure sheaf.

The finite-type condition supplies the covering family and, over each member, finitely many
sections of `ℐ` generating it, which are global sections of the slice structure sheaf generating
`ℐ|_{V_i}` on the nose
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal`); and for a
family of global sections the tag holds unconditionally
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isGlobalExtendedCech_idealOfGlobalSections`), applied to the
slice ringed site. -/
theorem exists_coversTop_isGlobalExtendedCech_overIdeal
    (hI : PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType X.J I.toSheafOfModules.val) :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (V : ι → X.C), X.J.CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i : ι, ∃ (K : CochainComplex
            (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over (V i)).O)) ℤ)
          (a : K ⟶ structureSheafComplex (X.over (V i))),
        IsGlobalExtendedCech (X.over (V i)) (overIdeal I (V i)) K a := by
  obtain ⟨ι, V, hV, hgen⟩ := exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal X I hI
  refine ⟨ι, V, hV, fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨n, gens, hgens⟩ := hgen i
  obtain ⟨K, a, hKa⟩ :=
    exists_isGlobalExtendedCech_idealOfGlobalSections (X.over (V i)) gens
  refine ⟨K, a, ?_⟩
  rw [hgens]
  exact hKa

/-- **The same, at Mathlib's finite-type condition** — the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 099E] —
turned into the sectionwise one by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteType`. -/
theorem exists_coversTop_isGlobalExtendedCech_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType
    [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (V : ι → X.C), X.J.CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i : ι, ∃ (K : CochainComplex
            (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over (V i)).O)) ℤ)
          (a : K ⟶ structureSheafComplex (X.over (V i))),
        IsGlobalExtendedCech (X.over (V i)) (overIdeal I (V i)) K a :=
  exists_coversTop_isGlobalExtendedCech_overIdeal X I
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteType I.toSheafOfModules inferInstance)

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
